.TH "PB-SERVICE-STATUS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-service-status - Show Paperboat daemon current-user service status


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb service status [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show Paperboat daemon current-user service status

.PP
Report whether the current-user daemon service is installed and running. Runtime readiness and account connectivity may require pb status or pb doctor as well.

.PP
Service commands manage the current user's background Paperboat daemon through the host operating system. The service runs pb daemon; it is not a separate Paperboat binary. Use status to inspect the supervised process and restart after a local configuration change.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-service(1)\fP
